Move /proc, /sys, /dev into /sysroot before switch_root

After `switch_root /sysroot /sbin/init`, the kernel exec's the new
init (Nerves: erlinit) in the new rootfs. erlinit then issues mount(2)
syscalls referencing /dev/mmcblk0p20p1, /dev/mmcblk0p20p3, etc.

Without `mount --move /dev /sysroot/dev` beforehand, busybox
switch_root tears down the initramfs's devtmpfs mount during the
pivot_root + umount cleanup. The new rootfs's own /dev (an empty
directory from the squashfs) is left in its place, so every
/dev/<block> reference erlinit makes fails with
`Can't lookup blockdev`, the init exits, and the kernel reboots
shortly after switch_root.

Mirror the postmarketOS / systemd pattern of moving the critical
virtual filesystems into the new root before switching.

--- a/initramfs/usr/share/citronics-initramfs/init
+++ b/initramfs/usr/share/citronics-initramfs/init
@@ -52,7 +52,18 @@
         # echo_kmsg "Restore consoles to original state..."
         # restore_consoles

-        echo_kmsg "Switching to /sysroot"
+        echo_kmsg "Moving /proc, /sys, /dev into /sysroot before switch_root"
+        # Without this, busybox switch_root unmounts our initramfs
+        # devtmpfs as it pivots, leaving the new root with an empty
+        # /dev. erlinit then can't resolve any /dev/<block> path and
+        # the kernel reboots.
+        mount --move /proc /sysroot/proc 2>/dev/null \
+            || echo_kmsg "  warn: /proc move failed"
+        mount --move /sys  /sysroot/sys  2>/dev/null \
+            || echo_kmsg "  warn: /sys move failed"
+        mount --move /dev  /sysroot/dev  2>/dev/null \
+            || echo_kmsg "  warn: /dev move failed"
+        echo_kmsg "Switching to /sysroot"
         exec switch_root /sysroot /sbin/init
     else
         echo_kmsg "Rootfs not mounted, launching debug_console..."
